  "description": "timing.v1 §2.7: one member's arrivals over a tool's window -> whether the period was kept. period_ms is the declared period; window.from_ms and window.to_ms the window's start and end on the tool's monotonic clock, in milliseconds; known whether the member is known (v1.md §0; to a tool, which holds no binding, only a member of a template without parameters, §2.7, text 0.3); ended_ms the instant the member ended within the window, or null; arrivals_ms the member's arrivals, ascending, exact to the nanosecond. The span starts at from_ms for a known member, else at the member's first arrival within the window (from_ms <= t <= to_ms), and ends at ended_ms when not null, else at to_ms. Its arrivals are those within the span, both ends included. expect.verdict is not_heard for a member not known with no arrival within the window (arrivals 0, span_ms null); too_short when the span is below 3 x period_ms; kept when (arrivals + 2) x period_ms is at least the span; not_kept otherwise. expect.arrivals is the count, expect.span_ms the span's length."
